<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Why Choose a Garage Floor Storm Shelter?</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Garage floor storm shelters are an excellent choice for homeowners in Sherman and the wider North Texas area who seek unobtrusive, permanent storm protection. Unlike above-ground safe rooms that occupy floor space, these units are installed beneath your garage floor, making them virtually invisible when not in use. This means you can continue to use your garage as normal, parking vehicles directly over the shelter.</p><p>The convenience of having a shelter readily accessible in your garage cannot be overstated, especially during sudden severe weather. You can quickly move from your home to safety without exposure to the elements. These shelters are built with robust steel construction, sliding hatch doors for easy access, and ventilation systems to ensure comfort and safety during a storm.</p><p>For more options, explore our <a href="/above-ground-safe-rooms/">above-ground safe rooms</a> or <a href="/underground-storm-shelters/">traditional underground storm shelters</a>.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Our Garage Shelter Installation Process</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>Installing a garage floor storm shelter requires specialized skills and equipment to ensure structural integrity and proper drainage. Our experienced team handles every step with precision:</p><ul><li><strong>Site Assessment:</strong> We evaluate your garage slab and identify the optimal placement for your shelter, considering utility lines and foundation specifics.</li><li><strong>Concrete Saw-Cutting:</strong> Our team uses professional-grade equipment to precisely cut and remove a section of your concrete garage floor.</li><li><strong>Excavation:</strong> We carefully excavate the soil to the required depth, preparing the cavity for the shelter unit.</li><li><strong>Shelter Placement:</strong> The pre-fabricated steel shelter is carefully lowered into the excavated space and leveled.</li><li><strong>Anchoring and Backfill:</strong> The shelter is securely anchored, and the surrounding area is backfilled with concrete or gravel to ensure stability.</li><li><strong>Concrete Finishing:</strong> We pour new concrete to fill the gap around the shelter, ensuring a seamless, flush finish with your existing garage floor.</li><li><strong>Cleanup:</strong> We ensure all debris is removed, leaving your garage clean and ready for use.</li></ul><p>We work efficiently to minimize disruption and complete your installation with the highest standards of craftsmanship. Learn more about typical <a href="/storm-shelter-cost/">storm shelter costs</a>.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Meeting Life-Safety Standards for Your Protection</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>At Texoma Storm Shelters, your safety is our top priority. All our garage floor storm shelters are designed and installed to meet or exceed stringent national safety guidelines. We adhere to the specifications outlined in:</p><ul><li><strong>FEMA P-320:</strong> This publication provides detailed guidance for constructing safe rooms for tornado and hurricane protection. Our shelters are built to withstand extreme wind forces and flying debris.</li><li><strong>ICC 500:</strong> The International Code Council (ICC) Standard for the Design and Construction of Storm Shelters offers comprehensive requirements for storm shelter performance. Our installations comply with these critical structural and occupant safety standards.</li></ul><p>By choosing a shelter that meets these standards, you are investing in a proven, tested solution for life-safety. We ensure every aspect of your installation provides the maximum protection possible against severe weather events common in North Texas. For more details, read our <a href="/blog/fema-icc-storm-shelter-standards/">guide on FEMA and ICC storm shelter standards</a>.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:0 24px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto 56px;">
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 18px;">Texoma Storm Shelters: Your Local Experts</h2>
    <div class="rich"><p>As a local, family-owned company, Texoma Storm Shelters is dedicated to serving communities across Sherman, Grayson, Fannin, and Cooke counties. We understand the unique weather challenges of our region and provide practical, reassuring solutions for your family's safety.</p><p>We offer free written estimates for all installations, ensuring transparent pricing with no hidden fees. Our team is licensed and insured, providing peace of mind from start to finish. When you choose us, you're partnering with authoritative life-safety experts committed to protecting your home and loved ones.</p><p>Contact us today at <a href="tel:+19038847210">(903) 884-7210</a> or email <a href="mailto:info@texomastormshelters.com">info@texomastormshelters.com</a> to discuss your garage floor storm shelter needs in Sherman, <a href="/storm-shelters-denison-tx/">Denison</a>, <a href="/storm-shelters-pottsboro-tx/">Pottsboro</a>, <a href="/storm-shelters-whitesboro-tx/">Whitesboro</a>, <a href="/storm-shelters-van-alstyne-tx/">Van Alstyne</a>, or <a href="/storm-shelters-gunter-tx/">Gunter</a>.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:72px 24px;background:#EAF5FB;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
