      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What is the typical cost for a garage floor storm shelter installation?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">The cost for a garage floor storm shelter installation in Sherman TX generally ranges from <strong>$4,800 to $7,900</strong>. This price includes the shelter unit, concrete saw-cutting, excavation, installation, and concrete finishing. Factors like shelter size and specific site conditions can affect the final estimate. We provide free written estimates to give you an accurate cost for your specific project.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">How long does it take to install a garage floor storm shelter?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Most garage floor storm shelter installations can be completed within one to two days. This includes the time needed for concrete cutting, excavation, placing the shelter, and finishing the concrete. We work efficiently to minimize disruption to your home. We'll provide a clear timeline with your free written estimate.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Can I really park my car over the shelter?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Yes, absolutely. Garage floor storm shelters are specifically designed to be flush-mounted into your concrete slab, allowing you to park your vehicle directly over them. The shelter's robust construction and the expert concrete finishing ensure it can safely support the weight of a standard vehicle without damage to the shelter or your garage floor.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">Do these shelters require any special maintenance?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Garage floor storm shelters require very little maintenance. We recommend periodically checking the sliding door mechanism to ensure it operates smoothly and cleaning out any debris that might accumulate inside. Proper drainage is built into the installation to prevent water issues. Our team can provide specific maintenance tips upon installation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What sizes are available for garage floor storm shelters?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Garage floor storm shelters come in various sizes to accommodate different family needs, typically ranging from 4-person to 12-person capacities. Common dimensions might include 4x6 feet, 5x7 feet, or larger. During your free consultation, we can discuss the best size for your family and garage space to ensure adequate protection.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
